  {"date": "2017-07-30", "venue": "Madison Square Garden", "city": "New York", "state": "NY", "gap": 14, "set": "2", "jamchart": true, "jam": "Moving beyond The Who classic, the jam initially settles into some  mellow, synth-infused grooving. Around 12:30, the sentiment brightens, and as the power builds, Trey unleashes some effects and trilling which recall the unique style and tone of '00. The jam gradually mellows into probing space.", "out": ">", "next": "A Song I Heard the Ocean Sing", "xprev": "David Bowie", "nb": 1},
  {"date": "2018-08-10", "venue": "Coastal Credit Union Music Park at Walnut Creek", "city": "Raleigh", "state": "NC", "gap": 28, "set": "2", "out": "->", "prev": "Meatstick", "in": ">", "next": "NICU", "nb": 1},
  {"date": "2019-12-28", "venue": "Madison Square Garden", "city": "New York", "state": "NY", "gap": 61, "set": "2", "jamchart": true, "jam": "The jam first turns for dark, goopy textures on the coattails of Page's synths and Trey's effects. Eventually, this yields way to a spirited \"Guy Forget\" quote driven by Fishman.", "out": ">", "prev": "Piper", "next": "Ass Handed", "nb": 1},
  {"date": "2021-08-14", "venue": "Atlantic City Beach", "city": "Atlantic City", "state": "NJ", "gap": 20, "set": "2", "jamchart": true, "jam": "While staying somewhat close to typical \"Drowned\" jamming, the music explores those bounds widely until 10:30, when there is a distinctive shift to new terrain. The jam becomes pulsing and percussive before finally settling to quiet transition space.", "out": ">", "prev": "I Never Needed You Like This Before", "next": "Ghost", "nb": 1},
